  "term": "fusion",
  "definition": "In historical psychology, fusion means that parts of an experience join because of similarity or other natural fit, so they are hard to tell apart or analyze separately. The stronger the fusion, the more the elements form a unified whole rather than a simple sum, though the term was used somewhat differently by different schools.",
